{"name":"Natural Habitat","hex":"#82745c","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"natural","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Existing in nature.","Normally associated with a particular person or thing; inherently related to the nature of a thing or creature."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A native inhabitant of a place, country, etc.","A note that is not or is no longer to be modified by an accidental."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/natural"},{"term":"habitat","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Conditions suitable for an organism or population of organisms to live.","A range; a place where a species naturally occurs."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/habitat"}],"entries":[{"title":"Habitat","blocks":[{"text":"In ecology, habitat refers to the array of resources, biotic factors that are present in an area, such as to support the survival and reproduction of a particular species. A species' habitat can be seen as the physical manifestation of its ecological niche. Thus \"habitat\" is a species-specific term, fundamentally different from concepts such as environment or vegetation assemblages, for which the term \"habitat-type\" is more appropriate."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Beech_Forest_%28AU%29%2C_Great_Otway_National_Park%2C_Beauchamp_Falls_--_2019_--_1271.jpg/330px-Beech_Forest_%28AU%29%2C_Great_Otway_National_Park%2C_Beauchamp_Falls_--_2019_--_1271.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Habitat","wikidata":"Q52105"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/4/4e/Beech_Forest_%28AU%29%2C_Great_Otway_National_Park%2C_Beauchamp_Falls_--_2019_--_1271.jpg/500px-Beech_Forest_%28AU%29%2C_Great_Otway_National_Park%2C_Beauchamp_Falls_--_2019_--_1271.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimed